    "body": "## Motivation\n\nWhen loading diffusion configuration files via `ServerArgs.load_config_file()` or `FlexibleArgumentParser._load_config_file()`, empty or comment-only YAML files load as `None`, while YAML lists / JSON arrays load as sequences. The downstream CLI merge logic assumes a mapping and crashes with `TypeError: 'NoneType' object is not iterable` or `TypeError: 'list' object is not a mapping`.\n\nThis PR adds root-level type validation to ensure configuration files contain a mapping at the root level, consistent with the existing SRT config merger.\n\n## Changes\n\n1. In `ServerArgs.load_config_file()`:\n   - Normalize `None` results (empty or comments-only YAML/JSON) to `{}`.\n   - Reject scalar and list/sequence root elements with a clear `ValueError` requiring a mapping/dictionary.\n2. In `FlexibleArgumentParser._load_config_file()`:\n   - Apply the same normalization (`None` -> `{}`) and dictionary validation.\n3. Added focused CPU unit tests in `test/registered/unit/multimodal_gen/test_diffusion_config_validation.py` covering:\n   - Valid YAML & JSON mappings\n   - Empty YAML\n   - Comments-only YAML\n   - `null` JSON\n   - YAML lists and JSON arrays (rejects with `ValueError`)\n   - Scalar roots (rejects with `ValueError`)\n   - Unsupported file extensions\n\nFixes #45182\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39375600119](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39375600119)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39375600121](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39375600121)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39375600042](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39375600042)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
